{
  "uid": "voteball-alerts",
  "title": "Service Health & Alerts",
  "tags": ["voteball", "alerts"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Critical firing",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 4, "h": 6},
      "description": "Watchdog and InfoInhibitor are excluded -- Watchdog always fires by design (Prometheus' own dead-man's-switch heartbeat, null-routed in addon-monitoring.tf) and InfoInhibitor is inhibition machinery, never a human-facing alert.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "red", "value": 1}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]},
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "count(ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\",severity=\"critical\",alertname!=\"Watchdog\",alertname!=\"InfoInhibitor\"}) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Warning firing",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 4, "y": 0, "w": 4, "h": 6},
      "description": "Watchdog and InfoInhibitor are excluded -- see the Critical firing panel for why.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "yellow", "value": 1}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]},
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "count(ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\",severity=\"warning\",alertname!=\"Watchdog\",alertname!=\"InfoInhibitor\"}) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Pending",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 8, "y": 0, "w": 4, "h": 6},
      "description": "Alerts whose condition is true but haven't been true for the alert's `for:` duration yet. count() over an empty set returns no data, not 0 -- the `or vector(0)` makes \"nothing pending\" render as an actual 0 rather than a blank tile.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "blue", "value": 1}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"]},
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "count(ALERTS{alertstate=\"pending\",alertname!=\"Watchdog\",alertname!=\"InfoInhibitor\"}) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Firing now",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 0, "w": 12, "h": 6},
      "description": "Every alert currently firing, from Prometheus' own ALERTS series (not Alertmanager -- see the Alertmanager panel in row 3 for what that adds).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "alertstate": true
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "alertname": 0,
              "severity": 1,
              "namespace": 2
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\",alertname!=\"Watchdog\",alertname!=\"InfoInhibitor\"}",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Availability vs 99% SLO",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 6, "w": 6, "h": 7},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0.9,
          "max": 1,
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {"mode": "line"}
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "red", "value": null},
              {"color": "green", "value": 0.99}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "voteball:availability:ratio5m",
          "legendFormat": "availability",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "p95 latency vs 1s SLO",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 6, "y": 6, "w": 6, "h": 7},
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "thresholdsStyle": {"mode": "line"}
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {"color": "green", "value": null},
              {"color": "red", "value": 1}
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "voteball:latency:p95_5m",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Journey request rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 12, "y": 6, "w": 6, "h": 7},
      "description": "This is the synthetic canary's traffic, not organic site traffic -- Voteball has close to no organic traffic, so zero here means the canary stopped (see VoteballJourneyTrafficStopped), not that the site is down.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {"unit": "reqps"},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "voteball:journey_requests:rate5m",
          "legendFormat": "requests",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Journey error rate",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 18, "y": 6, "w": 6, "h": 7},
      "description": "Errors from the canary's own synthetic voting journey -- the numerator behind VoteballHighErrorRate/VoteballAvailabilitySLOBreach.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {"unit": "reqps"},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "voteball:journey_errors:rate5m",
          "legendFormat": "errors",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Alert history, 6h",
      "type": "state-timeline",
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 0, "y": 13, "w": 16, "h": 8},
      "description": "From Prometheus' own ALERTS series, not Alertmanager -- Alertmanager only knows what is firing right now and has no history of its own. This is the only way to answer \"was this alert firing during last night's incident?\".",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {"unit": "short"},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mergeValues": true,
        "showValue": "never",
        "rowHeight": 0.9,
        "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom"}
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
          "expr": "ALERTS{alertstate=\"firing\",alertname!=\"Watchdog\",alertname!=\"InfoInhibitor\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{alertname}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Alertmanager -- delivered & silenced",
      "type": "text",
      "datasource": {"type": "alertmanager", "uid": "alertmanager"},
      "gridPos": {"x": 16, "y": 13, "w": 8, "h": 8},
      "description": "What this adds over the Alert history panel: grouping, silences and inhibition -- i.e. what was actually DELIVERED (grouped into one notification, or suppressed) versus what merely fired in Prometheus' ALERTS series.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Alertmanager -- delivered & silenced**\n\nThis panel wires up the `alertmanager` data source (uid `alertmanager`), provisioned by kube-prometheus-stack since day one and never referenced by any panel until now.\n\nWhat it adds over *Alert history* to the left: **grouping, silences and inhibition** -- i.e. what was actually **delivered** as a notification versus what merely **fired**. Alertmanager has no history of its own, only Prometheus' `ALERTS` series does (see the panel to the left); Alertmanager is the source of truth for *why you did or didn't get an email*.\n\nGrafana's built-in Alertmanager data source cannot be queried from a dashboard panel -- its `query()` is a stub that always returns empty data (confirmed against Grafana 13.1.1's own source, `public/app/plugins/datasource/alertmanager/DataSource.ts`), and the Alert List panel's Alertmanager picker only offers Grafana-managed alert-forwarding targets, not a data source of this plugin type (`grafana/grafana#108531`, closed *not planned*). Only Grafana's own Alerting pages call it, through a resource proxy the panel query model doesn't expose.\n\n**To see it live:** open **Alerting -> Alertmanager** in the Grafana left nav and choose **Alertmanager** from the picker at the top. That page shows active notifications, silences and the notification-policy tree for this cluster's real Alertmanager -- grouped and de-duplicated exactly as delivered."
      }
    }
  ]
}
